  "constraints": [
    "Preserve unused 40-pin signals as passthrough only. Pi 5V pins2/4 not connected to sensor circuitry. No I2C EEPROM or formal HAT+ compliance claimed.",
    "40pin stack needs appropriate header height/standoffs; cooler/component clearance and physical mounting not verified.",
    "Do not connect external3.3V supply when stacked. Power sensors only from Pi3.3V; prevent backfeed in standby.",
    "GPIO27 proposed because logicalGPIO17 is reserved for key state; verify GPIO27 is unused before connecting brake. No Pi config changes have been performed.",
    "Wake via40pin GPIO unsupported onPi5. J5 requires separate two-wire link toPiJ2; J6 dry momentary contact only. No3V3/5V/12V connection toJ5/J6; no ground tie on carrier.",
    "Fuel1k is a bench starting point, not tank calibration. Oil is identified as Dweekiy B07ZYWMV89 single-wire body-grounded; electrical curve/bias unknown, so J3 remains disconnected. Brake is factory99Miata reservoir isolated switch.",
    "Series resistors/caps optional; no automotive voltage fault/transient protection claimed. Sensor circuits isolated from old gauges/powered circuits.",
    "Insulated jumpers are soldered to underside pads beside the component lead; do not force multiple wire ends through a single hole. Bare buses are continuous straight tinned-wire runs soldered at listed taps. Crossovers must remain insulated.",
    "J5/J6 are passive parallel button-extension pads only. Disconnect or inspect the previously failed J2 circuit before adding a parallel contact; a stuck existing output can hold the button active.",
    "Existing module VDD bypass capacitor is relied upon; its value/connection not established from supplied stock photo. No duplicate carrier capacitor fitted by default.",
    "Rev C fits R1fuel/R5brake plus R7bleed/R8limiter/C6/D1 in wake corner. R3/C1/C2/F1/F2 optional analog components remain unpopulated and LK1/LK2 fitted. No duplicate supply capacitors or I2C pull-ups.",
    "C6 <=8mm diameter, R8 <=9mm body; actual fit in wake corner must be dry-fitted. All new trigger wires insulated; keep away from 40pin contacts.",
    "Do not connect J7 to HAT5V/3V3, raw12Vautomotivefeed, or continuouslylivebatteryoutput. Dedicatedregulatedchargertrigger only."
  ],
